              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\alpha,-\\alpha,\\beta",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and use the cubic root-coefficient relationships.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the roots be $\\alpha$, $-\\alpha$ and $\\beta$.\n\nFrom the sum of pairwise products,\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\alpha^2&=\\frac{-32}{2}\\\\\\alpha^2&=16\\end{align*}$$\nFrom the product of the roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\alpha^2\\beta&=-\\frac{-16}{2}\\\\-16\\beta&=8\\\\\\beta&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nFrom the sum of the roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\beta&=-\\frac{k}{2}\\\\-\\frac12&=-\\frac{k}{2}\\\\k&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe opposite roots are $4$ and $-4$. Thus $k=1$ and the roots are $4$, $-4$ and $-\\frac12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
